00:26:23.540 --> 00:26:25.660
I was like, how does he make it seem so natural?
我当时在想，他是怎么做到让表演看起来那么自然的？

663
00:26:26.360 --> 00:26:28.780
He's, I mean, Craig is really brilliant, guys.
他是，我是说，克雷格真的很棒，伙计们。

664
00:26:29.000 --> 00:26:29.920
He's super talented.
他非常有才华。

665
00:26:30.220 --> 00:26:31.660
Craig, come be on the podcaSt.
克雷格，来上我们的播客吧。

666
00:26:32.100 --> 00:26:33.160
I reached out to him.
我联系过他了。

667
00:26:33.160 --> 00:26:34.280
We've traded some messages.
我们交换过一些信息。

668
00:26:34.280 --> 00:26:35.180
It's going to happen.
这事儿会成的。

669
00:26:35.180 --> 00:26:36.820
We just have to figure out dates.
我们只需要确定一下时间。

670
00:26:37.040 --> 00:26:38.020
Let's lock it up, Craig.
把它定下来吧，克雷格。

671
00:26:38.220 --> 00:26:38.880
Let's lock it up.
把它定下来。

672
00:26:39.300 --> 00:26:46.700
Well, as Daryl is explaining the dangers of the bailer, for example, Michael is making a ton of jokes.
嗯，比如当达里尔在解释打包机的危险性时，迈克尔在开各种玩笑。

673
00:26:47.600 --> 00:26:49.580
Andy's trying to suck up to Dwight.
安迪在试图讨好德怀特。

674
00:26:49.780 --> 00:26:53.840
And this is when people start making bets, right?
而这时大家开始打赌了，对吧？

675
00:26:54.020 --> 00:26:54.300
Yes.
没错。

676
00:26:54.420 --> 00:26:56.540
This is the other storyline of the whole episode.
这是整集剧情的另一条故事线。

677
00:26:56.980 --> 00:27:02.960
So Daryl is about to say, do you know how many people lose an arm in a bailer each year?
所以达里尔正要说，你知道每年有多少人因为打包机失去手臂吗？

678
00:27:03.160 --> 00:27:06.620
Kevin and Jim decide to bet on what they think the answer is.
凯文和吉姆决定打赌他们认为答案是多少。

679
00:27:07.820 --> 00:27:08.500
Yes, exactly.
是的，没错。

680
00:27:08.700 --> 00:27:10.000
It happens around four minutes.
这发生在四分钟左右的时候。

681
00:27:10.240 --> 00:27:14.700
I want to share with you that Mindy said something that really made me laugh in the DVD commentary.
我想和你们分享一下，明迪在DVD评论音轨里说的一件事真的让我笑了。

682
00:27:14.960 --> 00:27:18.460
She said that in the writer's room, they were talking about this bailer.
她说在编剧室里，他们当时在讨论这台打包机。

683
00:27:18.720 --> 00:27:23.640
And they really saw it as a scary, big piece of machinery.
他们真的把它看作是一台可怕的大型机器。

684
00:27:23.960 --> 00:27:25.940
Like maybe it had blades or something.
就像它可能带有刀片之类的东西。

685
00:27:26.200 --> 00:27:29.720
And when they got it, she said it just looked like a big telephone booth.
而当他们拿到它时，她说它看起来就像个大电话亭。

686
00:27:31.040 --> 00:27:31.520
Yes.
没错。

687
00:27:31.520 --> 00:27:33.640
That moved really slowly.
而且移动得非常缓慢。

688
00:27:35.500 --> 00:27:42.500
Well, I talked to Kent Sabornak about this bailer, and he said that it was a real working bailer.
嗯，我和肯特·萨博纳克聊过这台打包机，他说那是一台真正能工作的打包机。

689
00:27:42.680 --> 00:27:43.200
Yeah.
是啊。

690
00:27:43.480 --> 00:27:45.740
We had an actual safety meeting.
我们还开过一次真正的安全会议。

691
00:27:45.900 --> 00:27:46.520
Remember, Jenna?
还记得吗，珍娜？

692
00:27:47.100 --> 00:27:47.360
Yes.
记得。

693
00:27:47.360 --> 00:27:51.780
When we went into the warehouse to shoot, our second AD held a safety meeting that was like,
当我们进入仓库拍摄时，我们的第二助理导演开了一个安全会议，内容大概是，

694
00:27:51.820 --> 00:27:53.060
guys, we have a forklift.
伙计们，我们有叉车。

695
00:27:53.140 --> 00:27:53.940
We have a bailer.
我们有打包机。

696
00:27:54.060 --> 00:27:55.060
Do not touch anything.
什么都别碰。

697
00:27:55.060 --> 00:27:57.600
Yeah, these are real machines.
是啊，这些都是真正的机器。

698
00:27:58.620 --> 00:28:04.360
He said that he called the manufacturer Olympic Wire and Equipment, and they donated a bailer
他说他给制造商Olympic Wire and Equipment打了电话，他们捐赠了一台打包机，

699
00:28:04.360 --> 00:28:09.800
because they got like free product placement so that we got a free bailer.
因为他们获得了免费的产品植入，所以我们得到了一台免费的打包机。

700
00:28:10.280 --> 00:28:18.300
Well, I want to say that there is this little part at the end of the bailer conversation where it's going on and on, right?
嗯，我想说的是，在打包机对话的最后有一小段内容，一直在没完没了地讲，对吧？

701
00:28:18.460 --> 00:28:18.600
Yeah.
是啊。

702
00:28:18.860 --> 00:28:21.400
And Daryl is like, so do you understand?
然后达里尔就说，你明白了吗？

703
00:28:21.560 --> 00:28:25.700
And Michael is like, yes, only on the rarest occasion.
迈克尔就说，明白，只在极少数情况下。

704
00:28:25.700 --> 00:28:30.760
And Daryl is like, on no occasions, on no occasions.
达里尔就说，任何情况下都不明白，任何情况下都不明白。

705
00:28:31.660 --> 00:28:35.380
I had to look that up in the script, and I will tell you that was not in the script.
我得去剧本里查查，我得告诉你，那句台词剧本里没有。

706
00:28:35.480 --> 00:28:36.680
I think that was improvised.
我觉得那是即兴发挥的。

707
00:28:36.880 --> 00:28:43.600
I feel like I remember that, too, being there, and we just let Steve and Craig go back and forth.
我感觉我也记得那段，当时我就在现场，我们只是让史蒂夫和克雷格在那儿一来一回地斗嘴。

708
00:28:44.080 --> 00:28:45.100
Just go back and forth.
就让他们一来一回地斗。

709
00:28:46.500 --> 00:28:48.680
And, you know, it brought me back, Angela.
而且，你知道吗，这让我回想起了过去，安吉拉。

710
00:28:48.880 --> 00:28:51.520
I just loved shooting this episode.
我特别喜欢拍这一集。

711
00:28:51.520 --> 00:28:57.880
And part of it was because, if you notice, we're all in these big group scenes almost all the time.
部分原因在于，如果你注意到了，我们几乎所有时间都在拍这些大型群戏。

712
00:28:58.600 --> 00:28:58.740
Yeah.
是啊。

713
00:28:59.360 --> 00:29:01.480
This was an episode of big group scenes.
这一集全是大型群戏。

714
00:29:01.600 --> 00:29:06.560
And not just that, we also got to work with Patrice and Craig and Carly.
不仅如此，我们还能和帕特里斯、克雷格还有卡莉一起合作。

715
00:29:06.700 --> 00:29:08.540
We had all the warehouse folks, too.
仓库里的伙计们也都在。

716
00:29:08.760 --> 00:29:10.420
We were all together all the time.
我们一直都在一起。

717
00:29:10.420 --> 00:29:12.260
And it really is rare.
这真的很难得。

718
00:29:12.400 --> 00:29:14.120
I mean, it happened in the basketball episode.
我是说，篮球那一集发生过这种情况。

719
00:29:14.120 --> 00:29:17.660
It happened in this one, some Christmas parties and things like that.
这一集也发生了，还有一些圣诞派对之类的场合。

720
00:29:17.760 --> 00:29:20.920
But it was rare, and we would all just have a great time.
但这很罕见，我们大家在一起总是玩得很开心。

721
00:29:21.540 --> 00:29:26.840
And I liked it, too, because it was such a simple idea.
我也很喜欢这一集，因为它构思非常简单。

722
00:29:26.980 --> 00:29:28.680
It's just safety training day.
就是安全培训日。

723
00:29:28.800 --> 00:29:29.060
I know.
我知道。

724
00:29:29.160 --> 00:29:29.600
That's it.
就这么简单。

725
00:29:29.720 --> 00:29:35.060
And it goes off the rails, and we're all in, like, all of us are now on this roller coaster.
然后事情就失控了，我们所有人都被卷了进来，就像坐上了过山车一样。

726
00:29:35.060 --> 00:29:35.580
Can't get any work done.
什么工作都干不了。

727
00:29:35.780 --> 00:29:35.920
Yeah.
是啊。

728
00:29:36.180 --> 00:29:41.980
Well, I have to say, before we leave the scene, I absolutely love that Michael cannot remember Madge's name.
好吧，我得说，在离开这个场景之前，我特别喜欢迈克尔记不住玛奇名字的那个桥段。

729
00:29:42.280 --> 00:29:43.120
He can't.
他就是记不住。

730
00:29:43.500 --> 00:29:43.920
No.
没错。

731
00:29:44.020 --> 00:29:46.300
He calls her Patch, Pudge.
他管她叫帕奇、帕奇（Pudge）。

732
00:29:46.620 --> 00:29:48.320
He cannot remember her name.
他就是记不住她的名字。

733
00:29:48.940 --> 00:29:53.300
My mom cannot remember a name that is just slightly different.
我妈也记不住那些稍微有点不一样的名字。

734
00:29:53.740 --> 00:29:54.820
Just slightly different.
就只是稍微有点不一样。

735
00:29:55.500 --> 00:29:56.380
Here's an example.
给你举个例子。

736
00:29:56.560 --> 00:30:00.760
When I was in college, my roommate's boyfriend's name was Bart.
我上大学的时候，我室友的男朋友叫巴特（Bart）。

737
00:30:01.320 --> 00:30:02.320
B-A-R-T.
B-A-R-T。

738
00:30:02.600 --> 00:30:02.720
Bart.
巴特。

739
00:30:03.300 --> 00:30:03.740
Okay.
好的。

740
00:30:03.900 --> 00:30:06.260
And the day I met him, my mom was with me.
我见到他的那天，我妈也在场。

741
00:30:06.340 --> 00:30:08.900
And the minute he was like, hi, I'm Bart.
他刚一说，你好，我是巴特。

742
00:30:08.920 --> 00:30:10.480
I thought, nope, not going to happen.
我就想，完了，这下完了。

743
00:30:10.960 --> 00:30:12.380
Nope, it's never going to get that one.
完了，她永远也记不住这个名字了。

744
00:30:12.540 --> 00:30:13.140
What did she call him?
她管他叫什么？

745
00:30:13.140 --> 00:30:16.600
For years, for years, she called him Mart.
好几年，整整好几年，她都管他叫马特（Mart）。

746
00:30:17.360 --> 00:30:17.960
How's Mart?
马特怎么样了？

747
00:30:18.420 --> 00:30:19.420
I'm like, mom, it's Bart.
我说，妈，他叫巴特。

748
00:30:19.700 --> 00:30:20.340
What'd I say?
我说什么了？

749
00:30:20.700 --> 00:30:21.660
You said Mart.
你说的是马特。

750
00:30:21.900 --> 00:30:22.360
I did?
我有吗？

751
00:30:22.600 --> 00:30:23.620
Yes, you did.
没错，你确实说了。

752
00:30:25.100 --> 00:30:25.580
Wow.
哇。

753
00:30:26.800 --> 00:30:28.940
But who would name their child Mart?
但谁会给孩子起名叫马特（Mart）呢？

754
00:30:29.260 --> 00:30:30.220
I don't know.
我不知道。

755
00:30:30.520 --> 00:30:31.380
I don't know.
我不知道。

756
00:30:31.500 --> 00:30:33.340
But, like, who would name their kid Patch?
但是，谁会给孩子起名叫帕奇（Patch）呢？

757
00:30:33.560 --> 00:30:34.460
Or Padge?
或者帕奇（Padge）？

758
00:30:34.620 --> 00:30:35.300
Or Pudge?
或者帕奇（Pudge）？

759
00:30:35.480 --> 00:30:36.360
It's like...
这就像是……

760
00:30:36.360 --> 00:30:37.520
You're so right.
你说得太对了。

761
00:30:37.520 --> 00:30:41.180
By the way, I apologize in advance for our listener named Mart.
顺便说一下，我先向我们那位叫马特的听众道个歉。

762
00:30:41.400 --> 00:30:43.760
I would also like to apologize to anyone named Patch.
我也想向所有叫帕奇的人道歉。

763
00:30:44.140 --> 00:30:44.900
Or Pudge.
或者叫帕奇的。

764
00:30:45.420 --> 00:30:47.600
Well, now we're going to go upstairs, Angela.
好了，现在我们要上楼了，安吉拉。

765
00:30:48.240 --> 00:30:50.620
Toby is going to teach his safety meeting.
托比要开始他的安全会议了。

766
00:30:51.180 --> 00:30:55.960
For whatever reason, Michael has forced everyone from the warehouse to come to this presentation.
不管出于什么原因，迈克尔强迫仓库里的每个人都来参加这次演讲。

767
00:30:56.260 --> 00:30:58.880
Paul Lieberstein knocks this out of the park.
保罗·利伯斯坦这次表现得太棒了。

768
00:30:59.040 --> 00:31:03.780
As great as Daryl was in the warehouse, Paul is as Toby in the office.
达里尔在仓库里有多棒，保罗在办公室里演托比就有多棒。

769
00:31:04.080 --> 00:31:04.520
Yes.
是的。

770
00:31:04.520 --> 00:31:07.380
His list of things, guys, to be prepared for.
伙计们，他列出的那些需要防范的事情。

771
00:31:07.600 --> 00:31:08.340
Are you ready for them?
你们准备好听了吗？

772
00:31:09.300 --> 00:31:10.840
Toby's office safety training.
托比的办公室安全培训。

773
00:31:11.380 --> 00:31:12.680
Carpal tunnel syndrome.
腕管综合征。

774
00:31:13.880 --> 00:31:14.760
Poor circulation.
血液循环不良。

775
00:31:15.820 --> 00:31:18.200
Computer, screen, eye strain.
电脑、屏幕、眼睛疲劳。

776
00:31:18.900 --> 00:31:22.380
And you might want to keep a sweater or a cardigan in case it gets drafty.
你可能想准备一件毛衣或开衫，以防有穿堂风。

777
00:31:23.480 --> 00:31:23.680
Yeah.
没错。

778
00:31:24.740 --> 00:31:26.020
Michael is so frustrated.
迈克尔太沮丧了。

779
00:31:26.340 --> 00:31:27.480
He can't take it.
他受不了了。

780
00:31:27.480 --> 00:31:31.340
None of these things are as exciting as getting your arm cut off in a bailer.
这些事情哪有在打包机里被切断手臂那么刺激。

781
00:31:31.420 --> 00:31:32.140
He can't take it.
他受不了了。

782
00:31:32.140 --> 00:31:37.160
At 5 minutes, 52 seconds, Ryan says, what about a long-sleeved tee?
在5分52秒时，瑞安问，那长袖T恤怎么样？

783
00:31:37.900 --> 00:31:38.280
Yeah.
没错。

784
00:31:38.720 --> 00:31:40.080
Here's a great story about that.
关于这个有个很棒的故事。

785
00:31:40.460 --> 00:31:46.360
According to BJ, there was a huge joke debate about that line, what about a long-sleeved tee?
据BJ说，关于那句台词“那长袖T恤怎么样”，当时有一场巨大的争论。

786
00:31:46.660 --> 00:31:48.060
And at 2 a.m.
而且是在凌晨两点。

787
00:31:48.100 --> 00:31:49.740
in the writer's room, they were debating it.
在编剧室里，他们还在争论。

788
00:31:49.920 --> 00:31:53.120
Mike Schur said, no, this is a ridiculous line.
迈克·舒尔说，不，这台词太荒谬了。

789
00:31:53.160 --> 00:31:55.180
And Greg was all for it.
但格雷格非常支持。

790
00:31:58.180 --> 00:32:01.220
This is so funny that they spent time debating this line.
他们花时间争论这句台词真是太搞笑了。

791
00:32:01.620 --> 00:32:01.760
I know.
我知道。

792
00:32:01.960 --> 00:32:02.320
I know.
我知道。

793
00:32:02.440 --> 00:32:03.580
I love this line.
我喜欢这句台词。

794
00:32:03.840 --> 00:32:04.480
Me too.
我也是。

795
00:32:04.500 --> 00:32:06.040
And it gets called back later.
而且后来还有呼应。

796
00:32:06.040 --> 00:32:06.400
I know.
我知道。

797
00:32:06.660 --> 00:32:07.500
When we're asked to go downstairs.
当我们被要求下楼的时候。

798
00:32:07.920 --> 00:32:07.970
I know.
我知道。

799
00:32:08.100 --> 00:32:08.600
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

800
00:32:10.460 --> 00:32:14.240
Well, maybe that's why BJ delivered it so wryly.
嗯，也许这就是为什么BJ说得那么戏谑。

801
00:32:15.480 --> 00:32:16.460
It got in.
它被收录了。

802
00:32:16.660 --> 00:32:20.280
He knew the backstory of this debate in the writer's room over that line.
他知道编剧室里关于那句台词的幕后故事。

803
00:32:20.480 --> 00:32:24.780
We had a fan question about another line in this little bit.
我们收到一个粉丝提问，是关于这一小段里的另一句台词。

804
00:32:25.060 --> 00:32:25.220
Okay.
好的。

805
00:32:26.400 --> 00:32:35.120
Sarah Bell, Dagny Albano, and Katie Boyd all asked, when Michael's reading the safety booklet and he says office life causes a sedimentary lifestyle.
Sarah Bell、Dagny Albano 和 Katie Boyd 都问到，当迈克尔读安全手册时，他说办公室生活会导致“沉积式”生活方式。

806
00:32:35.880 --> 00:32:37.980
Was that improv or was that in the script?
那是即兴发挥还是剧本里写的？

807
00:32:38.140 --> 00:32:39.740
That was not in the script.
那不是剧本里的。

808
00:32:39.920 --> 00:32:40.560
You're kidding.
你开玩笑吧。

809
00:32:41.100 --> 00:32:47.880
There's a little bit of banter there between Michael and Toby that looks like it veered a little bit off script, like they were having a little fun with it.
迈克尔和托比之间有一点互动，看起来有点脱离剧本了，就像他们在那儿玩得很开心一样。

810
00:32:48.000 --> 00:32:48.820
Oh, I love that.
哦，我喜欢那个。

811
00:32:49.020 --> 00:32:50.280
So, Michael has had it.
所以，迈克尔受够了。

812
00:32:50.420 --> 00:32:51.320
He takes over.
他接手了。

813
00:32:51.480 --> 00:32:54.000
He's like, Toby, I'm going to do the safety training.
他说，托比，我要来做安全培训。

814
00:32:54.280 --> 00:32:58.360
And he wants to show the warehouse people that working in an office is just as dangerous.
他想向仓库员工证明，在办公室工作也同样危险。

815
00:32:59.360 --> 00:33:02.500
And he says, oh, there's seasonal affective disorder.
他说，哦，还有季节性情绪失调。

816
00:33:02.880 --> 00:33:04.940
Like dim light can lead to depression.
就像昏暗的灯光会导致抑郁一样。

817
00:33:05.620 --> 00:33:07.720
And the warehouse people, they're out.
而仓库员工们，他们不买账。

818
00:33:07.940 --> 00:33:09.840
They're like, yeah, dim light's a bitch.
他们觉得，是啊，昏暗的灯光真是个大麻烦。

819
00:33:09.840 --> 00:33:14.800
