我要和你们分享一下。

983
00:39:52.860 --> 00:40:03.860
So they talked about in the commentary that originally the idea was that everyone went up on the roof to talk Michael out of this.
他们在评论音轨里提到，最初的想法是让所有人都上屋顶去劝迈克尔放弃这个念头。

984
00:40:04.620 --> 00:40:05.180
Everyone.
所有人。

985
00:40:05.400 --> 00:40:05.480
Oh.
噢。

986
00:40:05.640 --> 00:40:05.800
Yeah.
是啊。

987
00:40:06.140 --> 00:40:13.380
And Harold was like, I don't think it really sells how serious, like what he's contemplating.
哈罗德当时说，我觉得这样表现不出事情的严重性，或者说他到底在考虑什么。

988
00:40:13.380 --> 00:40:23.160
I think if he's on the roof and he's shouting down to everyone in the parking lot and you have that whip camera panning from the roof back to him and down and up,
我觉得如果他在屋顶上，对着停车场里的所有人大喊，再加上那种从屋顶到他身上，再向下又向上的快速摇镜头，

989
00:40:23.320 --> 00:40:28.080
you really get the sense of what a horrible idea this is.
你就能真正感受到这是一个多么糟糕的主意。

990
00:40:28.680 --> 00:40:30.320
Yeah, that was Harold.
没错，那是哈罗德的主意。

991
00:40:30.480 --> 00:40:33.320
Harold was like, no, guys, everyone else should be in the parking lot.
哈罗德当时说，不，伙计们，其他所有人都应该在停车场里。

992
00:40:33.540 --> 00:40:34.800
Only Michael on the roof.
只有迈克尔在屋顶上。

993
00:40:35.000 --> 00:40:36.480
I just thought that was really great.
我当时就觉得这真的很棒。

994
00:40:36.740 --> 00:40:44.420
Well, I know that they probably wanted us up on the roof because technically it would be easier to shoot with sound and camera.
嗯，我知道他们可能想让我们都上屋顶，因为从技术上讲，那样拍摄声音和画面会更容易。

995
00:40:44.420 --> 00:40:48.140
It was it was such a technically difficult episode.
那集在技术上真的太难拍了。

996
00:40:48.140 --> 00:40:49.340
And I remember that.
我记得这一点。

997
00:40:49.480 --> 00:40:57.420
I remember how difficult it was for them to get angles on all of us and him and the bright sun and the sound.
我记得他们要拍到我们所有人、拍到他，还要应对刺眼的阳光和收音问题，有多么困难。

998
00:40:57.960 --> 00:41:04.880
Kudos to our crew because it doesn't seem like it was difficult, but it was actually really technically difficult.
向我们的剧组致敬，因为看起来好像并不难，但实际上在技术上真的非常困难。

999
00:41:05.280 --> 00:41:05.420
Yeah.
是啊。

1000
00:41:05.600 --> 00:41:09.420
And to Steve and the guys that were on the roof, just the limited crew up there with him.
还有史蒂夫和在屋顶上的那些人，毕竟只有有限的工作人员能和他一起上去。

1001
00:41:09.580 --> 00:41:11.860
They were up on that roof for a really long time.
他们在那个屋顶上待了真的很久。

1002
00:41:12.520 --> 00:41:12.720
Yeah.
是啊。

1003
00:41:12.720 --> 00:41:14.080
Yeah, yeah, they were.
没错，确实是。

1004
00:41:14.260 --> 00:41:17.300
Well, now back in the office, the whole betting game is still going.
好了，现在回到办公室，整个打赌游戏还在继续。

1005
00:41:17.540 --> 00:41:22.980
People are placing bets on how long it's going to take Kelly to explain to Ryan how Netflix works.
大家都在下注，赌凯莉要花多久才能给瑞安解释清楚奈飞是怎么运作的。

1006
00:41:23.180 --> 00:41:29.180
They're betting like how many times she's going to say the word awesome and and what movie she mentions and how long it takes.
他们赌她会说多少次“太棒了”，会提到哪部电影，以及要花多长时间。

1007
00:41:29.360 --> 00:41:30.060
It's it's heated.
场面非常激烈。

1008
00:41:30.940 --> 00:41:35.160
Yes, we find out that Kelly talked for two minutes and 42 seconds.
没错，我们发现凯莉一共讲了两分四十二秒。

1009
00:41:35.540 --> 00:41:42.020
She said the word awesome 12 times and mentioned six romantic comedies and never had a clue.
她说了十二次“太棒了”，提到了六部浪漫喜剧，而且完全没察觉到状况。

1010
00:41:42.020 --> 00:41:45.080
As people were like putting money on the table next to Ryan.
当时大家都在瑞安旁边的桌子上放钱。

1011
00:41:45.720 --> 00:41:50.500
Well, we had a fan question from Elizabeth Myers, who says old tech alert.
我们收到了伊丽莎白·迈尔斯的一个粉丝提问，她说：老科技警报。

1012
00:41:51.100 --> 00:41:53.820
Can you guys explain this Netflix scene?
你们能解释一下这个奈飞场景吗？

1013
00:41:53.960 --> 00:41:54.880
What is a cue?
什么是队列（cue）？

1014
00:41:55.800 --> 00:41:57.120
What is a cue?
什么是队列？

1015
00:41:57.360 --> 00:41:58.300
You guys.
你们这些人啊。

1016
00:41:59.780 --> 00:42:01.920
Yes, I didn't even think of that.
没错，我甚至都没往那方面想。

1017
00:42:02.100 --> 00:42:04.020
You remember old Netflix, right, Angela?
安吉拉，你还记得老版奈飞吧？

1018
00:42:04.340 --> 00:42:04.760
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
记得，记得，记得。

1019
00:42:04.840 --> 00:42:08.640
You'd put it in your cue like it was like a list of what you were going to watch.
你会把它放进你的队列里，就像是一个你打算观看的清单。

1020
00:42:09.440 --> 00:42:11.960
Because you got a DVD in the mail.
因为你是通过邮寄收到DVD的。

1021
00:42:12.320 --> 00:42:12.460
Yeah.
是啊。

1022
00:42:12.680 --> 00:42:14.460
It didn't just come up on your TV.
它不是直接出现在你的电视上的。

1023
00:42:14.460 --> 00:42:20.100
So you would have to go to the Netflix website and pick what DVDs you want them to send to you.
所以你必须去奈飞网站，挑选你想让他们寄给你的DVD。

1024
00:42:20.280 --> 00:42:21.720
And you could pick the order.
而且你可以选择顺序。

1025
00:42:22.180 --> 00:42:28.340
And then when you were done watching it, you put it in this like prepaid postage envelope and you sent it back.
当你看完之后，把它放进那个预付邮资的信封里寄回去。

1026
00:42:28.680 --> 00:42:33.220
And whenever they got the one that you sent back, they would send you the next one in your cue.
每当他们收到你寄回的那张，他们就会寄给你队列里的下一张。

1027
00:42:33.220 --> 00:42:36.820
Yeah, it was like a mail-in blockbuster, basically.
没错，基本上就像是邮寄版的百视达。

1028
00:42:37.520 --> 00:42:43.420
It was revolutionary because the idea was you didn't have to drive to the video store anymore to rent your videos.
这在当时是革命性的，因为它的理念是你再也不用开车去录像带店租片子了。

1029
00:42:43.620 --> 00:42:49.820
The problem was, though, sometimes you'd be like waiting for your next thing to come up in your cue.
不过问题是，有时候你会一直等着队列里的下一部片子寄过来。

1030
00:42:50.180 --> 00:42:50.340
Yeah.
是啊。

1031
00:42:51.040 --> 00:43:01.940
So, lady, this whole Netflix cue thing, it reminded me of how my parents got the DVD mail Netflix service for like ever.
所以，这位女士，这个奈飞队列的事情让我想起我父母用那个DVD邮寄服务用了好久好久。

1032
00:43:01.940 --> 00:43:03.100
For like ever.
真的用了好久。

1033
00:43:03.260 --> 00:43:05.440
They would not switch to the streaming one.
他们就是不肯换成流媒体服务。

1034
00:43:05.620 --> 00:43:05.820
Why?
为什么？

1035
00:43:05.920 --> 00:43:06.900
Why wouldn't they switch?
他们为什么不换？

1036
00:43:07.840 --> 00:43:09.000
I don't know.
我不知道。

1037
00:43:09.320 --> 00:43:11.920
But they did the DVD thing forever.
但他们确实用了好久的DVD服务。

1038
00:43:12.380 --> 00:43:14.240
And I texted them about it.
我为此给他们发了短信。

1039
00:43:14.340 --> 00:43:15.140
I had to know.
我必须得问清楚。

1040
00:43:15.300 --> 00:43:17.300
And their responses were so funny.
他们的回复太搞笑了。

1041
00:43:17.340 --> 00:43:18.800
And my mom said I could share them.
我妈说我可以分享出来。

1042
00:43:18.960 --> 00:43:19.280
Okay.
好的。

1043
00:43:19.720 --> 00:43:22.560
So you said, what did you, wait, what did you text them?
那你说了什么，等等，你给他们发了什么短信？

1044
00:43:22.560 --> 00:43:33.200
I texted, hey guys, how long ago did you switch from the old Netflix service of getting physical DVDs in the mail to getting the streaming service?
我发的是：嘿，爸妈，你们是从多久以前开始从那种邮寄实体DVD的老版奈飞服务，切换到流媒体服务的？

1045
00:43:33.440 --> 00:43:33.620
Okay.
好的。

1046
00:43:34.280 --> 00:43:36.280
They texted me back separately.
他们分别给我回了短信。

1047
00:43:36.500 --> 00:43:36.900
Okay.
好的。

1048
00:43:37.380 --> 00:43:37.600
Okay.
好的。

1049
00:43:38.040 --> 00:43:42.200
My dad texted me back, don't remember, quite a while.
我爸回我说：不记得了，挺久以前了吧。

1050
00:43:42.640 --> 00:43:43.080
Okay.
好的。

1051
00:43:43.960 --> 00:43:44.500
The end.
结束了。

1052
00:43:45.940 --> 00:43:51.240
My mom texted back, dad's mowing the lawn, but I think I can help you.
我妈回短信说，我爸在割草，但我想我可以帮你。

1053
00:43:53.340 --> 00:43:55.760
Maybe that's why his text was so brief.
也许这就是他短信回得那么简短的原因。

1054
00:43:56.860 --> 00:43:58.100
Yeah, I think so.
是啊，我也这么觉得。

1055
00:43:58.240 --> 00:43:58.720
It made sense.
这说得通。

1056
00:43:59.260 --> 00:43:59.520
Okay.
好吧。

1057
00:43:59.520 --> 00:44:09.160
And then she said, a while back I was having lunch with a friend and she told me that we could get Netflix the cable channel for $9.95 a month.
然后她说，前阵子我和朋友吃午饭时，她告诉我我们可以以每月9.95美元的价格订购Netflix有线频道。

1058
00:44:09.620 --> 00:44:13.180
We were paying that just to get two movies a month in the mail.
我们之前每个月花同样的钱，却只能通过邮寄收到两部电影。

1059
00:44:13.380 --> 00:44:16.500
So that's when we signed up and dropped our other plan.
所以我们就在那时注册了Netflix，并取消了原来的套餐。

1060
00:44:17.020 --> 00:44:22.440
It's funny because I had wanted to get Netflix on cable, but dad kept telling me it was too expensive.
真有意思，因为我本来一直想订购有线电视版的Netflix，但我爸总说太贵了。

1061
00:44:22.740 --> 00:44:24.720
I mean, you know how dad is about money.
你知道的，我爸对钱一向很看重。

1062
00:44:25.240 --> 00:44:34.780
So, we've had Netflix streaming for, I'd say, three years now, but dad does not like it when you have to pay extra for certain movies.
所以，我们用Netflix流媒体服务大概有三年了，但我爸不喜欢那种看特定电影还要额外付费的模式。

1063
00:44:34.980 --> 00:44:39.880
I really want to watch the movie Fatima, but you have to pay for it and he won't do it.
我真的很想看《法蒂玛》这部电影，但需要付费，他肯定不肯。

1064
00:44:39.980 --> 00:44:42.340
But I will once again win this battle.
但我会再次赢得这场博弈的。

1065
00:44:42.520 --> 00:44:43.480
You know how it works.
你知道这套流程的。

1066
00:44:43.820 --> 00:44:45.200
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1067
00:44:45.940 --> 00:44:47.580
That is so layered.
这信息量也太大了。

1068
00:44:47.880 --> 00:44:49.880
That is so jam-packed with information.
简直是干货满满。

1069
00:44:49.940 --> 00:44:52.680
First of all, I love that she's like, dad is mowing.
首先，我喜欢她说“我爸在割草”那段。

1070
00:44:53.160 --> 00:44:57.380
Then, I love that she's like, a while back, I was having lunch.
然后，我也喜欢她说“前阵子，我在吃午饭”那段。

1071
00:44:57.500 --> 00:44:59.700
Because you're like, wait, where are we going?
因为你会想，等等，我们要去哪儿？

1072
00:44:59.860 --> 00:45:00.460
What's happening?
发生什么事了？

1073
00:45:00.480 --> 00:45:00.940
I know.
我知道。

1074
00:45:01.420 --> 00:45:02.200
I know.
我知道。

1075
00:45:02.600 --> 00:45:03.620
But, yes.
但是，没错。

1076
00:45:03.860 --> 00:45:09.120
So, I guess three years, only three years ago, my parents were still getting DVDs in the mail.
所以，我想大概三年前，仅仅三年前，我父母还在通过邮寄收DVD。

1077
00:45:09.240 --> 00:45:14.960
And I remember because I would ask them, you know, I would be like, they were in love with Downton Abbey.
我记得很清楚，因为我会问他们，你知道的，他们当时特别迷《唐顿庄园》。

1078
00:45:15.120 --> 00:45:15.740
Downton Abbey.
《唐顿庄园》。

1079
00:45:15.840 --> 00:45:18.240
And I'd be like, what season are you on?
我会问，你们看到第几季了？

1080
00:45:18.320 --> 00:45:20.320
And they're like, well, we're waiting for the next season.
他们会说，哦，我们在等下一季。

1081
00:45:20.320 --> 00:45:21.340
It hasn't come yet.
还没寄到呢。

1082
00:45:21.340 --> 00:45:23.160
Yes, it's right there.
没错，它就在那儿。

1083
00:45:23.380 --> 00:45:24.240
Just subscribe.
直接订阅就行了。

1084
00:45:24.560 --> 00:45:25.860
It's right there.
它就在那儿。

1085
00:45:26.360 --> 00:45:26.760
Yeah.
是啊。

1086
00:45:26.920 --> 00:45:27.580
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1087
00:45:27.740 --> 00:45:29.000
They're waiting for their DVD.
他们还在等他们的DVD。

1088
00:45:29.240 --> 00:45:30.480
That is amazing.
这太神奇了。

1089
00:45:31.440 --> 00:45:31.980
All right.
好吧。

1090
00:45:32.080 --> 00:45:36.040
Should we take a break and then come back and talk about those watermelons on the roof?
我们要不要休息一下，回来再聊聊屋顶上的那些西瓜？

1091
00:45:36.260 --> 00:45:36.660
Yes.
好。

1092
00:45:36.780 --> 00:45:40.000
And I have some good info from Kentopedia about the watermelons.
而且我从“肯特百科”那里得到了一些关于西瓜的好消息。

1093
00:45:40.140 --> 00:45:41.360
Well, I want to hear it.
嗯，我很想听听。

1094
00:45:41.560 --> 00:45:41.820
All right.
好的。

1095
00:45:41.920 --> 00:45:42.000
Good.
太好了。

1096
00:45:42.040 --> 00:45:42.680
We'll be right back.
我们马上回来。

1097
00:45:42.940 --> 00:45:52.040
All right.
好的。

1098
00:45:52.240 --> 00:45:53.020
So, we are back.
我们回来了。

1099
00:45:53.380 --> 00:45:55.120
Dwight and Michael are on the roof.
德怀特和迈克尔在屋顶上。

1100
00:45:55.120 --> 00:46:02.540
And they are testing sort of an experiment to see how far Michael has to jump out to land on the trampoline.
他们正在进行一项实验，看看迈克尔必须跳多远才能落在蹦床上。

1101
00:46:02.760 --> 00:46:06.380
And they've got some watermelons and they're giving it a go.
他们拿了一些西瓜，正准备试一试。

1102
00:46:06.680 --> 00:46:10.400
So, lady, I reached out to Kentopedia because I had two questions.
所以，女士，我联系了“肯特百科”，因为我有两个问题。

1103
00:46:11.720 --> 00:46:18.020
Number one, I wanted to know how did Steve and Rain get up on the roof and who all was up there with them?
第一，我想知道史蒂夫和雷恩是怎么爬上屋顶的，还有谁和他们一起在上面？

1104
00:46:18.180 --> 00:46:20.400
Did they have to ride that thing that you and John rode?
他们必须坐你和约翰坐的那种东西吗？

1105
00:46:20.960 --> 00:46:21.360
Yes.
是的。

1106
00:46:21.540 --> 00:46:25.760
They had to use that big scissor lift and everyone had to wear a safety harness.
他们必须使用那个大型剪叉式升降机，而且每个人都必须穿上安全带。

1107
00:46:26.320 --> 00:46:31.040
But here was something new that Kent added this season.
但肯特这一季增加了一些新东西。

1108
00:46:31.500 --> 00:46:40.980
Kent hired some stunt guys to rig safety cable up on the roof of the stage so that if there was ever a time where the crew had to be up there to do lighting,
肯特雇了一些特技人员在舞台屋顶上安装了安全缆绳，这样如果剧组人员需要上去布置灯光，

1109
00:46:41.240 --> 00:46:46.240
they would be able to wear a safety harness and clip themselves onto a safety cable.
他们就能穿上安全带，把自己扣在安全缆绳上。

1110
00:46:46.240 --> 00:46:53.020
So, for this scene, Steve and Rain and Randall, who was our cinematographer,
所以，对于这场戏，史蒂夫、雷恩和我们的摄影指导兰德尔，

1111
00:46:53.340 --> 00:46:59.680
they all had safety harnesses underneath their costumes and they were clipped onto the safety cable as well.
他们都在戏服里面穿了安全带，并且也都扣在了安全缆绳上。

1112
00:46:59.800 --> 00:47:09.320
So, that also probably involved the wardrobe department because she would have had to have made sure their suits were big enough to go over the safety harness.
所以，这可能也涉及到了服装部门，因为她必须确保他们的戏服足够大，能套在安全带外面。

1113
00:47:10.060 --> 00:47:10.700
Yes.
是的。

1114
00:47:10.940 --> 00:47:14.460
I also had a question about the watermelons.
我还有一个关于西瓜的问题。

1115
00:47:15.000 --> 00:47:15.620
Oh, okay.
哦，好的。

1116
00:47:15.620 --> 00:47:17.400
And I was not alone.
而且不止我一个人有疑问。

1117
00:47:18.800 --> 00:47:29.540
Lauren Brightwell, Megan Keel, Ciara Begley, Phoebe Bono, and Maddie McKee all wanted to know how many watermelons were used for the trampoline test scene.
劳伦·布莱特韦尔、梅根·基尔、西亚拉·贝格利、菲比·博诺和麦迪·麦基都想知道蹦床测试那场戏用了多少个西瓜。

1118
00:47:29.900 --> 00:47:30.680
How many?
用了多少个？

1119
00:47:31.180 --> 00:47:38.260
Kent told me that we purchased 12 watermelons, but around take 10, Kent said to Harold Ramis,
肯特告诉我我们买了12个西瓜，但在拍到第10条时，肯特对哈罗德·雷米斯说，

1120
00:47:38.800 --> 00:47:47.200
I think we're going to need to CGI the watermelon thing because none of the watermelons that he was throwing off the roof were coming anywhere close to hitting the car.
我想我们得用电脑特效来处理西瓜那段，因为他从屋顶扔下来的西瓜没有一个能接近砸中那辆车。

1121
