you can see a great view of the impound lot across the street with all the trains.
你可以看到街对面扣押车辆停车场的一览无余的景色，还有所有的火车。

1162
00:50:01.620 --> 00:50:03.120
I noticed it too.
我也注意到了。

1163
00:50:03.440 --> 00:50:03.760
Yeah.
是啊。

1164
00:50:03.980 --> 00:50:06.400
You get a real slice of where we were, guys.
你们能真切地感受到我们当时在哪里，伙计们。

1165
00:50:06.600 --> 00:50:10.120
Those were our neighbors when we filmed at Chandler Valley Studios.
那是我们在钱德勒谷摄影棚拍摄时的邻居。

1166
00:50:10.480 --> 00:50:10.940
Yeah.
没错。

1167
00:50:12.100 --> 00:50:16.580
And one last thing from this watermelon moment, because I just thought it was so sweet.
关于这个西瓜片段还有最后一件事，因为我觉得这太温馨了。

1168
00:50:16.580 --> 00:50:21.780
BJ, in the commentary, said that this was one of those moments, Jenna.
BJ在评论音轨里说，这是那种时刻之一，珍娜。

1169
00:50:22.060 --> 00:50:27.600
It reminded me of when you talk about being on the roof, eating that grilled cheese sandwich
这让我想起你谈到在屋顶上吃那个烤奶酪三明治的时候，

1170
00:50:27.600 --> 00:50:30.180
on that warm, beautiful night, right?
在一个温暖美好的夜晚，对吧？

1171
00:50:30.480 --> 00:50:31.880
It was like that for BJ.
对BJ来说也是那种感觉。

1172
00:50:32.080 --> 00:50:35.280
He said, I had this moment where I was like, wait a second.
他说，我当时有那么一瞬间心想，等一下。

1173
00:50:35.540 --> 00:50:40.420
I'm on a roof with Steve Carell and Rainn Wilson and Harold Ramis.
我正和史蒂夫·卡瑞尔、雷恩·威尔森还有哈罗德·雷米斯在屋顶上。

1174
00:50:40.420 --> 00:50:44.240
We're throwing watermelons and I'm getting paid.
我们在扔西瓜，而且我还在拿工资。

1175
00:50:44.780 --> 00:50:45.220
Yes.
是的。

1176
00:50:45.340 --> 00:50:46.600
I thought that was so sweet.
我觉得这太甜了。

1177
00:50:46.820 --> 00:50:51.040
That's what made me think of the Dude Perfect thing because I was like, these are like a bunch
这就是让我想起“完美老兄”组合的原因，因为我觉得，这就像一群哥们儿在屋顶上往下扔西瓜，玩得很开心，但噢，他们是在工作。

1178
00:50:51.040 --> 00:50:56.760
of dudes up on a roof throwing watermelons down, just having a great time, but oh, they're
就像一群哥们儿在屋顶上往下扔西瓜，玩得很开心，但噢，他们是在工作。

1179
00:50:56.760 --> 00:50:57.180
at work.
是在工作。

1180
00:50:57.320 --> 00:50:57.540
Yeah.
是啊。

1181
00:50:58.020 --> 00:50:59.460
Like that was their job that day.
就像那是他们那天的工作一样。

1182
00:50:59.480 --> 00:51:00.580
I mean, how fun.
我是说，多好玩啊。

1183
00:51:00.780 --> 00:51:01.700
So fun.
太好玩了。

1184
00:51:02.060 --> 00:51:05.140
Well, I have some more news about this scene before we move on.
好吧，在继续之前，关于这个场景我还有些消息。

1185
00:51:05.140 --> 00:51:05.420
Okay.
好的。

1186
00:51:05.680 --> 00:51:07.920
The car that they hit was a rental.
他们砸的那辆车是租来的。

1187
00:51:08.820 --> 00:51:11.740
It was a Chrysler 300 picture car.
那是一辆克莱斯勒300道具车。

1188
00:51:12.640 --> 00:51:15.260
Guess how much money it cost them to do this gag?
猜猜他们做这个恶作剧花了多少钱？

1189
00:51:15.760 --> 00:51:16.860
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

1190
00:51:16.980 --> 00:51:17.900
I don't know.
我不知道。

1191
00:51:18.100 --> 00:51:18.720
How much?
多少钱？

1192
00:51:19.360 --> 00:51:24.160
They dented the roof and they broke the electric moon roof of the car.
他们砸凹了车顶，还弄坏了车的电动天窗。

1193
00:51:24.260 --> 00:51:25.460
From that one watermelon?
就因为那一个西瓜？

1194
00:51:25.900 --> 00:51:26.500
Yeah.
是的。

1195
00:51:26.680 --> 00:51:28.840
It cost $6,500 to fix it.
修好它花了6500美元。

1196
00:51:29.240 --> 00:51:29.480
Dang.
天哪。

1197
00:51:30.040 --> 00:51:30.500
Yeah.
是啊。

1198
00:51:32.120 --> 00:51:32.900
All right.
好吧。

1199
00:51:33.000 --> 00:51:34.360
Should we move back inside?
我们回到室内继续吗？

1200
00:51:34.360 --> 00:51:39.120
Yes, because I texted Creed Bratton about this next scene.
好的，因为我给克里德·布拉顿发了短信，问了关于下一个场景的事。

1201
00:51:39.320 --> 00:51:41.000
The betting is continuing.
赌局还在继续。

1202
00:51:41.580 --> 00:51:44.840
Everyone is watching Creed eat his apple.
大家都在看克里德吃苹果。

1203
00:51:45.220 --> 00:51:46.060
Creed doesn't know.
克里德毫不知情。

1204
00:51:46.160 --> 00:51:47.200
They're all standing behind him.
他们都站在他身后。

1205
00:51:47.380 --> 00:51:48.900
He sets the apple down.
他把苹果放下了。

1206
00:51:49.520 --> 00:51:52.440
Jim walks by, puts a potato where the apple was.
吉姆走过来，把一个土豆放在了刚才放苹果的地方。

1207
00:51:53.080 --> 00:51:59.320
Will Creed notice he's now eating a potato and not an apple?
克里德会发现他现在吃的是土豆而不是苹果吗？

1208
00:51:59.520 --> 00:52:01.260
Well, we got mail about this, Angela.
嗯，我们收到了关于这件事的邮件，安吉拉。

1209
00:52:01.260 --> 00:52:08.220
Bianca H., Kayla O., Cassidy Price, Deanna Horn, and Merrilee S.
比安卡·H、凯拉·O、卡西迪·普莱斯、迪安娜·霍恩和梅里莉·S。

1210
00:52:08.420 --> 00:52:12.260
all asked, did Creed really take a bite out of a potato?
她们都问，克里德真的咬了一口土豆吗？

1211
00:52:13.140 --> 00:52:14.240
Uh, yeah.
呃，是的。

1212
00:52:14.540 --> 00:52:15.600
I texted him.
我给他发了短信。

1213
00:52:15.740 --> 00:52:16.660
This is what he said.
这是他说的。

1214
00:52:16.660 --> 00:52:17.160
What did he say?
他说了什么？

1215
00:52:17.420 --> 00:52:18.300
This is what he said.
这是他说的。

1216
00:52:18.660 --> 00:52:23.220
He wrote, I definitely bit right into that potato and it wasn't half bad.
他写道：我确实直接咬了那个土豆，味道还不错。

1217
00:52:24.000 --> 00:52:26.700
Oh, so there you go.
哦，所以就是这样。

1218
00:52:26.880 --> 00:52:27.960
There you go.
就是这样。

1219
00:52:28.520 --> 00:52:41.020
Well, Angela, it makes sense to me because in French, the word for apple is pom and the word for potato is pom de terre, which means apple of the earth or apple of the ground.
嗯，安吉拉，我觉得这说得通，因为在法语里，苹果是pom，而土豆是pom de terre，意思是大地之果或地上的苹果。

1220
00:52:41.500 --> 00:52:42.020
I'm sorry.
抱歉。

1221
00:52:42.120 --> 00:52:42.840
What is your logic?
你的逻辑是什么？

1222
00:52:43.120 --> 00:52:50.600
It makes sense to you that Creed would eat a potato and not know it wasn't an apple because it's the French word is pom de terre?
你觉得克里德会吃土豆却不知道那不是苹果，是因为法语里土豆叫pom de terre？

1223
00:52:51.520 --> 00:52:51.640
Yeah.
是啊。

1224
00:52:51.940 --> 00:52:52.120
Okay.
好吧。

1225
00:52:53.380 --> 00:52:55.920
Potato in Indonesian is kintang.
印尼语里的土豆是kintang。

1226
00:52:56.200 --> 00:52:57.400
What's apple?
那苹果呢？

1227
00:52:57.600 --> 00:52:58.680
Apple is appel.
苹果是appel。

1228
00:52:59.240 --> 00:52:59.480
Oh.
哦。

1229
00:52:59.700 --> 00:53:05.140
Well, the French have related the apple and the potato in their language.
嗯，法国人在他们的语言里把苹果和土豆联系在了一起。

1230
00:53:05.140 --> 00:53:05.620
Okay.
好吧。

1231
00:53:05.920 --> 00:53:11.760
And so perhaps, perhaps they, I don't know, they're onto something.
所以也许，也许他们，我不知道，他们发现了什么门道。

1232
00:53:12.000 --> 00:53:13.880
Perhaps Creed would do well in France.
也许克里德在法国会过得不错。

1233
00:53:14.840 --> 00:53:16.640
Yeah, I guess that's right.
是啊，我想你说得对。

1234
00:53:16.640 --> 00:53:19.780
But as long as he doesn't try to pick them up himself at a market.
但前提是他别去市场自己挑土豆。

1235
00:53:20.160 --> 00:53:21.260
And thump them.
还要去敲一敲它们。

1236
